# runaway route — the way out of a location is walked, and anybody on it stands in the way
#
# Arriving is shown on the map: the party comes in from the location's way in (the arena-exit glyph
# out in the map's margin) to the area it is entered by. Leaving goes back out the same way, along
# the ways it knows. A RUNAWAY rolls in every area of that walk where somebody confronts the party:
# a success walks on to the next, a failure stops it there and the narration resumes in that area.
# The area RUNAWAY is pressed in is not one of those stops: its roll is the narration's own, and a
# failure there starts the fight (enemy) or the confrontation (witness), as it always did.
#
# The track from the field runs past the yard to the rock, so the way back out from the rock is
# Rock → Yard → Field (where the location was entered). The brewer is put in the rock and the weaver
# in the yard, both hostile (`hostile`): getting away from the brewer then walks into the weaver.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --observe-only "Field–Rock Track"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# The arrival walked in from the way in.
expect-state map walk in to Test Field

strategy succeed
goal follow_path
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect Moved to: Test Rock

observe none
hostile brewer Test Rock
hostile weaver Test Yard
click button
advance 12 180
expect RUNAWAY
expect-state where Test Rock

# Away from the brewer: the dice settle, then the second roll is set to fail before the walk on.
click button
wait
click continue
strategy fail-dice
wait
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-state map walk from Test Rock to Test Yard
expect-state where Test Yard
expect after trying to run away
expect RUNAWAY
expect-no-state dialogue caught_red_handed

# From here it is the narration's own RUNAWAY again, and failing that one is what it always was: the
# weaver is an enemy, so the fight starts.
strategy fail-dice
click button
wait
click continue
wait mode Fighting 90

quit
